# Rohde Ecotop 60 Corner Thermal & Airflow Simulator (`kiln_thermal_sim`)

A coupled steady-state radiative, convective, conductive, and buoyant-plume
simulation tool for evaluating heat shield dimensions, floor insulation stacks,
and ventilation requirements for a cylindrical top-loading ceramics kiln
installed in a masonry corner.

---

## 1. System Requirements & Debian Package Dependencies

This project is designed for Debian Linux and relies exclusively on packages
from the standard Debian `main` archive (`apt`). Installing Python packages via
`pip` / PyPI is intentionally avoided.

Install all runtime, build, and test dependencies via `apt`:

```bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y \
    python3 \
    python3-absl \
    python3-numpy \
    python3-scipy \
    python3-protobuf \
    protobuf-compiler \
    python3-pytest \
    bazel \
    elpa-protobuf-mode
```

To ensure Bazel uses the system Python 3 interpreter and resolves Debian's
`/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages`, include the following `.bazelrc` in the
workspace root:

```text
build --action_env=PATH="/usr/bin:/bin"
build --action_env=PYTHONPATH="/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages"
test --test_env=PYTHONPATH="/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages"
```

